Looking at the code, the comment asks me to express that when the range is valid (which `checkRange` enforces: `fromIndex >= 0`, `toIndex >= 0`, and `fromIndex <= toIndex`), every bit in `[fromIndex, toIndex)` is flipped from its original value.

I'll use `\old(this.get(i))` to capture the original value and assert each bit is now its complement.

<code>assert (fromIndex >= 0 && toIndex >= 0 && fromIndex <= toIndex) => (\forall int i; fromIndex <= i && i < toIndex; this.get(i) == !\old(this.get(i)));</code>
